00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:21.170
And by the way, the real issue is when are
we talking about a person?

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:22.170
Not when life begins.

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:27.580
I mean, no one would deny that a clump of
cells is a form of life.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:30.380
The relevant question is, are we talking about
a person?

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.610
And if it's a person, does it get due process?

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:33.830
Does it get citizenship?

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:35.500
Does it get child support?

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:37.690
Can you get the child tax credit when you're
pregnant?

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:41.570
You know, all these other things that are
really about personhood rather than life.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:49.610
But imagine that science said, hey, life begins
at nine weeks and six days into the gestational

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:50.950
